"],["Caesar salad","dish/caesar-salad"],["Chicken Kiev","dish/chicken-kiev"],["Chrain","dish/chrain"],["Dressed herring","dish/dressed-herring"],["Forshmak","dish/forshmak"],["Goulash","dish/goulash"],["Gugelhupf","dish/gugelhupf"],["Kachka (restaurant)","dish/kachka-restaurant"],["Karelian pasty","dish/karelian-pasty"],["Kasha","dish/kasha"],["Khrenovina sauce","dish/khrenovina-sauce"],["Kolach (bread)","dish/kolach-bread"],["Kringle","dish/kringle"],["Medovukha","dish/medovukha"],["Mimosa salad","dish/mimosa-salad"],["Mors (drink)","dish/mors-drink"],["Nesselrode pudding","dish/nesselrode-pudding"],["Okroshka","dish/okroshka"],["Olivier salad","dish/olivier-salad"],["Pancake","dish/pancake"],["Paska (bread)","dish/paska-bread"],["Pâté","dish/pate"],["Pie","dish/pie"],["Pirozhki","dish/pirozhki"],["Polonaise sauce","dish/polonaise-sauce"],["Potato pancake","dish/potato-pancake"],["Pozharsky cutlet","dish/pozharsky-cutlet"],["Rassolnik","dish/rassolnik"],["Sauerkraut","dish/sauerkraut"],["Shchi","dish/shchi"],["Solyanka","dish/solyanka"],["Sorrel soup","dish/sorrel-soup"],["Soured milk","dish/soured-milk"]]}]},"ingredient/crangon-crangon":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/crangon-crangon","n":"Crangon crangon","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Crangon crangon is a species of caridean shrimp found across the northeastern Atlantic Ocean. Its range extends from the White Sea in the north of Russia to the coast of Morocco, including the Baltic Sea, and appears also throughout the Mediterranean and Black Seas. Commercially important, it is fished mainly in the southern North Sea. Common names include brown shrimp, common shrimp, bay shrimp, and sand shrimp, while translation of its French name crevette grise (or its Dutch equivalent grijze garnaal) sometimes leads to the English version grey shrimp. The generic and specific names derive from krangṓn (κραγγών), an Ancient Greek word for shrimp."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-crangon-crangon"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crangon_crangon"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["British cuisine","cuisine/british-cuisine",[["Potted shrimps","dish/potted-shrimps"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Nutmeg","ingredient/nutmeg"]]}]},"ingredient/whipped-topping":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/whipped-topping","n":"Whipped topping","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Whipped cream, also known as Chantilly cream or crème Chantilly, is high-fat dairy cream, known as heavy cream, whipping cream or double cream, that is aerated by whisking until it becomes light, fluffy, and capable of holding its shape. This process incorporates air into the cream, creating a semi-solid colloid. It is commonly sweetened with white sugar and often flavored with vanilla. Whipped cream is often served on desserts and hot beverages and used as an ingredient in desserts."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-whipped-topping"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whipped_topping"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine",[["Strawberry delight","dish/strawberry-delight"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Cracker","ingredient/cracker"],["Cream cheese","ingredient/cream-cheese"],["Gelatin","ingredient/gelatin"],["Gelatine dessert","ingredient/gelatine-dessert"],["Graham cracker","ingredient/graham-cracker"],["Strawberry","ingredient/strawberry"],["Whipped cream","ingredient/whipped-cream"]]}]},"dish/tekwan":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/tekwan","n":"Tekwan","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Tekwan is a soup dish originating from the Indonesian region of Palembang. The dish contains small fish cakes made of local Musi river fish similar to pempek, and is served with savory shrimp broth, rice vermicelli, mushrooms, and sliced jicama, sprinkled with sliced fresh celery, scallions, and fried shallots."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-tekwan"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tekwan"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine"],["Palembang cuisine","cuisine/palembang-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":11,"links":[["Broth","ingredient/broth"],["Celery","ingredient/celery"],["Edible mushrooms","ingredient/edible-mushrooms"],["Egg white","ingredient/egg-white"],["Fish cake","ingredient/fish-cake"],["Fishcake","ingredient/fishcake"],["Sago","ingredient/sago"],["Scallion","ingredient/scallion"],["Shallot","ingredient/shallot"],["Shrimp","ingredient/shrimp"],["Vermicelli","ingredient/vermicelli"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Daily Cooking Quest","ref":"site/dailycookingquest-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"dailycookingquest.com","note":"Indonesian home cook Anita's blog with a large archive of Indonesian recipes.","url":"https://dailycookingquest.com/cuisines/indonesian.html","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Indonesian cuisine","links":[["Arem-arem","dish/arem-arem"],["Arsik","dish/arsik"],["Asam pedas","dish/asam-pedas"],["Ayam goreng","dish/ayam-goreng"],["Ayam goreng kalasan","dish/ayam-goreng-kalasan"],["Ayam panggang","dish/ayam-panggang"],["Ayam Taliwang","dish/ayam-taliwang"],["Bajigur","dish/bajigur"],["Bakakak hayam","dish/bakakak-hayam"],["Bakpia","dish/bakpia"],["Bakwan","dish/bakwan"],["Bekasang","dish/bekasang"],["Betutu","dish/betutu"],["Bika ambon","dish/bika-ambon"],["Binte biluhuta","dish/binte-biluhuta"],["Bir pletok","dish/bir-pletok"],["Bolu kukus","dish/bolu-kukus"],["Botok","dish/botok"],["Brem","dish/brem"],["Bubur kacang hijau","dish/bubur-kacang-hijau"],["Bubur ketan hitam","dish/bubur-ketan-hit